//! # Original address ranges
//!
//! * `0x80142580..0x80145C50` (5 functions, 796 bytes, coverage band A) -
//!   promoted from `src/subsystems/r80140_80180.rs`; that staging file now
//!   holds no code. `0x80144030` [`wm_update_held_item`] joined this group in
//!   the final pass, once the held-object role was accepted as inferred.
//! * `0x801025D0..0x80106FA0` (15 functions, 1,348 bytes, clusters D-E of lane
//!   `r80100_80140`) - promoted in a second pass; that staging file now holds
//!   no code. Cluster D is the `0x55`-entry WorldMap effect-slot table; cluster
//!   E is shared transform math (see below).
//! * Wave 3 second pass reads `main.dol` `0x80103220..0x801040D0`,
//!   `0x80142510..0x801472D0` and `0x8014F3D0..0x8014FD60`. All twenty-five
//!   functions are new ledger rows; no address in this group was translated
//!   before wave 3.
//! * Wave 4 reads `0x801025C0..0x80106E60`: the `0x34`-byte effect pool, the
//!   effect-id tables that feed it, the record dispatchers, and three
//!   transform-record helpers. Twenty-five functions, 5,948 bytes. Wave 4 also
//!   corrects the parameter order of [`wm_effect_slot_alloc`] (see the note in
//!   its doc comment).
//! * Wave 5 reads `0x80145980` and `0x8014B060..0x8014C690`: the WorldMap
//!   player actor constructor, three release entry points, one transform
//!   helper, sixteen state/update handlers and one shared vector helper.
//!   Twenty-two functions, 3,940 bytes. The cluster uses the same
//!   `+0x14A4` state word, `+0x14D8` target object and `+0x1520` attach handle
//!   as the interaction code in `src/game/interaction.rs`; the actor identity is
//!   supported by the `WM_PLAYER` string in `main.elf` and by the
//!   `Wm_mr_yssweatrun` effect emitted by [`wm_player_sweat_effect`].
//! * Wave 9 reads `0x8014A260..0x8014AFC0` and `0x8014E4E0..0x80150AB0`:
//!   the `0xD70`-byte WorldMap map-object constructor and its refresh/exit
