// Wave 19: WorldMap spin/landing states, target selection and transform resets
// ===========================================================================
//// This pass continues the `0x80100000..0x80140000` lane in address order:
//// * `0x80106FC0` / `0x80107020` close the transform-record cluster that wave 4
//   started at `0x80106DF0`: one applies a 100-byte scene record and commits
//   the inline transform at `+0x1C`, the other restores the renderer's
//   channel state.
// * `0x801298B0..0x8012DE20` are WorldMap player action gates and target
//   selectors. They read the controller mode at `+0x154`, the spin timer at
//   `+0x2534`, the status-bit words at `+0x1014`, and resolve the current
//   target through `0x80162D00`.
// * `0x80134AB0` and `0x8013D1E0..0x8013E470` drive the spin/landing state:
//   entry animation, sub-object release, the four-player exit choice, and the
//   global/per-player flag byte at `r13-0x5988`.
//// Every address and byte size comes from `functions.tsv`. One callee,
// `0x8005F900`, is declared `void` by Ghidra even though the caller tests its
// `r3` result (the same convention as wave 12's ground probe), so that call
// keeps the returned word through `platform::call1`.
/// `0x80424558`: shared renderer/scene object passed to `0x801C9940`.
const G_80424558: usize = 0x8042_4558;
