// Wave 102 - `0x80120000` bucket remainder
//// This pass fills 26 of the 40 entries that were still untranslated in the
// `0x80120000` bucket after wave 96. Four clusters are covered:
//// * `0x801200C0..0x80121990` - the early fall/splash actor. It keeps its
//   two-state ground machine in `+0x360` with the timer `+0x5CC`, the bounce
//   scale `+0x5C8`, the contact word `+0x5C0` and the probed ground height
//   `+0x5F4`, and selects its per-kind drop from the `0x802F4CA0` table
//   indexed by `+0x618`.
// * `0x80125670..0x80125F70` - the per-player ground placement pair that eases
//   `+0x3AC`/`+0x3B4`/`0x3B8`/`0x3BC`/`0x3C0` through `0x8015F140`, selects
//   its targets from the `0x802F4D6C..0x802F4E04` tables by the pad-mode byte
//   at `r13 - 0x56E0 + 0x20`, and the small `+0x392` slot-class test.
// * `0x80126A80..0x8012B440` - the spin/jump state ladder on `+0x14A4`, the
//   `+0xEA4` sub-controller, the water/swim ladder (`+0x14A8`, `+0x2A70`,
//   `+0x1A18..+0x1A24`) and the four `0x80370xxx` field-condition tables.
// * `0x8012B5B0..0x8012FB10` - the water-entry step (`+0x1A1C`, `+0x1A20`),
//   the look-up pass (`+0x484`), the grab/impact distance (`+0x27D0`) and the
//   `+0x1569` splash helpers.
//// Every body keeps the literal Ghidra operands. `unaff_r2` is `SDA2_BASE`// (`0x80433080`) and `unaff_r13` is `SDA_BASE` (`0x8042F680`); the offsets this
// pass introduces are declared below with a `W102_` prefix so they cannot
// collide with the earlier passes' names.
