// ===========================================================================
// Wave 106 - `0x80110000` bucket remainder
//// The last 17 untranslated entries of the assigned `0x80110000` bucket. They
// split into three groups:
//// * `0x80110B60..0x80111850` - the `Fg3d_balloon` actor: the four-point rail
//   gate, the balloon contact response and the two G3D model sets
//   (`balloon`/`float`, `balloon_back`/`float_back`, and the optional
//   `I_kinoko` set selected by `+0x7EC`).
// * `0x801126A0..0x8011AFC0` - the ground-grid controller: the 4x2 probe
//   fan, the per-cell tile builder, the row builder, the full grid rebuild,
//   and the nearest-candidate/matrix placement passes.
// * `0x8011C750..0x8011DAB0` - the grid box tests and the ice-object spin
//   handlers. These previously stayed untranslated because their exports use
//   `GQR3`; the GQR value is now known (see the note below).
// * `0x801406F0..0x80147700` - the WorldMap player's motion/visibility helpers:
//   the slip actor's four-state warp countdown, the pose/scale blend, the
//   contact hand-off, the two `0x27E8` slot retire paths, the nearest-player
//   scan and the pose-table/effect selectors. They read the `0x802F4EF8`,
//   `0x802F4F18`, `0x802F50A8` and `0x80325260` tables and the `+0x60` actor
//   vtable.
// * `0x8014A690..0x8014F630` - the map-object side of the bucket: the two
//   `0x802DCBFC` dispatch wrappers, the `0x800541C0` quad multiply, the
//   warp-cannon flash step, the guarded `+0x400` forwarder and the target
//   state/effect switch. `0x801469D0` remains a deliberate skip (see
