// ===========================================================================
// Wave 110: goal-manager and warning-manager state-table initialisers
//
// The two large functions are static initialisers: they fill an array of
// 0x40-byte state records, construct each record's name through 0x8015F7C0,
// install the class vtable and copy a nine-word handler table from the data
// segment. Each record's 0xC-byte registration descriptor sits at
// `record - 0x10` (the free tail of the previous record); the first goal
// record uses `table - 0xC` because there is no previous record.
//
// The group also carries the 0x80103410 thunk onto the translated slot
// allocator.
//
// The handler-table words at 0x80322450.. / 0x80322A18.. are data-segment
// values that Ghidra prints as DAT_/PTR_ labels only, so their individual
// roles stay `// unknown:`; the copy order is literal.
// ===========================================================================

/// Forwards all seven arguments to [`wm_effect_slot_alloc`].
///
/// A 16-byte tail branch with no stack frame is register-transparent, so it
/// uses the target's already-reconstructed signature `(base, tag, p3..p7)`
/// rather than a newly invented one. Ghidra prints the call with no operands
/// because it could not recover the dropped argument registers.
///
/// # Original
/// - Ghidra: `FUN_80103410` at `0x80103410` (16 bytes)
/// - Evidence: `work/ghidra/main-gb/export/80103410_FUN_80103410.c`
///
/// # Arguments
/// * `base` - first slot record; forwarded unchanged.
/// * `tag` - effect id; `0x2F` is the empty marker.
/// * `p3`, `p4`, `p5`, `p6`, `p7` - slot fields.
///
/// # Returns
/// Nothing.
///
/// # Side effects
/// Exactly those of [`wm_effect_slot_alloc`].
///
/// # Safety
/// `base` must be writable for `0x55 * 0x150 + 1` bytes.
///
/// # Confidence
/// medium - the branch target is literal; the parameter list is inherited from
/// the target body, which wave 3 reconstructed from `r3`/`r4` and the stores.
pub unsafe fn fn_80103410(
    base: usize,
    tag: u32,
    p3: u32,
    p4: u32,
    p5: u32,
    p6: u32,
    p7: u32,
) {
    wm_effect_slot_alloc(base, tag, p3, p4, p5, p6, p7);
}

/// `0x8015F7C0`: constructs a state record name.
///
/// Writes the shared state-record base vtable `0x80328A18` at `+0x00`, the
/// name pointer at `+0x04` and a per-instance sequence number at `+0x08`.
const W110_FUN_8015F7C0: usize = 0x8015_F7C0;
