// | `0x80326C48` | `+0x14E8` | `0x80326C48..0x80326C60` | `0x80326C48`/`C4C` | `0x80326C50..0x80326C58` | 301-303 | 3 |
// | `0x80326C60` | `+0x14EC` | `0x80326C60..0x80326C78` | `0x80326C60`/`C64` | `0x80326C68..0x80326C74` | 307-310 | 4 |
//
// `0x80326C5C` (slot 304) is one padding word after the three-method table, not
// a header. The arithmetic closes exactly: 34 words = 10 + 10 + 3 + 4 methods
// (27 function words) + six header words + one padding word (7 null words).
// The three-header split is literal in [`wm_player_init`]'s constructor
// `0x8014B2F0`: it stores `0x80326C18` at `+0x14E0`, `0x80326C48` at `+0x14E8`
// and `0x80326C60` at `+0x14EC`, hands `(+0x14E4, +0x14E8)` to `0x8015FC90`,
// and then overwrites `+0x14E0` with `0x80326BE8` (`laneB_disasm.txt`, store
// window `0x8014B344..0x8014B384`). So the live vtable at `+0x14E0` has **ten**
// methods; slots 287/288 are the next table's header, not its slots 10/11.
//
// ## The 18 distinct targets
//
// | target | slots | owner | bytes | role |
// |---|---|---|---:|---|
// | `0x8014B510` | 277 | [`wm_player_dispose_b`] (tabled) | 100 | release `+0x18`, then the object |
// | `0x80153310` | 278, 290 | [`fn_80153310`] (wave 247) | 16 | `+0x18` member dispatch `+0xC` |
// | `0x8014ECF0` | 279, 291 | [`fn_8014ecf0`] (wave 247) | 16 | `+0x18` member dispatch `+0x10` |
// | `0x80153320` | 280, 292 | [`fn_80153320`] (wave 247) | 16 | `+0x18` member dispatch `+0x14` |
// | `0x8014ED20` | 281, 293 | [`fn_8014ed20`] (wave 247) | 16 | `+0x18` member dispatch `+0x18` |
// | `0x80153330` | 282, 294 | [`fn_80153330`] (wave 247) | 16 | `+0x18` member dispatch `+0x1C` |
// | `0x80153340` | 283, 295 | [`fn_80153340`] (wave 247) | 16 | `+0x18` member dispatch `+0x20` |
// | `0x80153350` | 284, 296 | [`fn_80153350`] (wave 248) | 16 | `+0x18` member dispatch `+0x24` |
// | `0x8014EFA0` | 285, 297 | [`fn_8014efa0`] (wave 248) | 16 | `+0x18` member dispatch `+0x28` |
// | `0x80153360` | 286, 298 | [`fn_80153360`] (wave 248) | 16 | `+0x18` member dispatch `+0x2C` |
// | `0x8014B4B0` | 289 | [`wm_player_dispose_a`] (tabled) | 96 | release `+0x18`, then the object |
// | `0x8014B470` | 301 | [`wm_player_free`] (tabled) | 64 | guarded release of the object |
// | `0x80153240` | 302 | [`fn_80153240`] (wave 248) | 96 | `+0xC` attach probe |
// | `0x801532A0` | 303 | [`fn_801532a0`] (wave 248) | 12 | clear the out-word |
// | `0x8014B430` | 307 | [`fn_8014b430`] (wave 248) | 64 | guarded release returning `this` |
// | `0x801532B0` | 308 | [`fn_801532b0`] (wave 248) | 28 | forward through `[this+8]` to `+0x28` |
// | `0x801532D0` | 309 | [`fn_801532d0`] (wave 248) | 28 | forward through `[this+8]` to `+0x2C` |
// | `0x801532F0` | 310 | [`fn_801532f0`] (wave 248) | 28 | forward through `[this+8]` to `+0x30` |
//
// The 27 function words collapse to 18 distinct targets because slots 290-298
// repeat slots 278-286 word for word; slots 287/288, 299/300 and 304-306 are
// the null words above. Nine of the ten methods of the `0x80326BE8` table are
// the `lwzu r12,0x18(r3)` member-dispatch family owned by
// [`b247_member_vcall0`]; slot 289 is its destructor.
//
// ## Coverage
//
// **27/27 function words already have exactly one Rust owner, so this pass
// translates nothing new.** The 15 untabled targets landed in wave 247 lane B
// (slots 278-283) and wave 248 lane B (284-286, 302-303, 307-310); the three
// tabled words are the `translated` ledger rows for [`wm_player_free`],
// [`wm_player_dispose_a`] and [`wm_player_dispose_b`]; the nine alias words
// reuse those same owners. No table word in the span is uncovered.
//
// Evidence: `work/wave250/laneB_dump.mjs` (raw words),
// `work/wave250/laneB_census.mjs` (slot/owner/tsv census) and
// `work/wave250/laneB_dis.mjs` (recursive descent). All 18 targets were walked
// again in `work/wave250/laneB_disasm.txt`; every existing body matches its
// instructions, and the constructor store window confirms the four-table
// partition. The 18 bodies total 660 B.

// ===========================================================================
// `0x80325878` secondary block (wave 248, lane A, `_A248`)
// ===========================================================================
//
// The next structure after the world-map actor table `0x80325428`, and the
// table the wave 247 lane D report handed to this pass. Ghidra names the address
// `DAT_80325878`, and the map-object constructor [`fn_801442b0`] stores it at
// object `+0x14FC` (`lis r4,0x8032` / `addi r4,r4,0x5878` / `stw r4,0x14FC(r30)`),
// so this is the secondary vtable of the embedded sub-object that
// [`fn_80135fc0`], [`fn_80136000`], [`fn_80136650`] and friends pass to
// `0x800D2200`/`0x800D2270` as `(object + 0x14FC)`.
//
// The vtable follows the CodeWarrior layout already used by `0x80325420` and
// `0x80329958`: two zero words at the base (offset-to-top and RTTI, both `0`),
// then the method slots from `+8`. Slot 0 is `0x80325880 -> 0x801446A0`; there
// is **no second method slot**. The 50 words from `0x80325884` to `0x80325948`
// are a zero run, exactly the padding the wave 248 lane B report describes
// before the `0x80326D0C` descriptor array.
//
// The rest of the block is *not* a vtable. From `0x8032594C` the data is an
// array of 12-byte `{key, value, pad}` records:
//   * `{name_offset, 0x60, 0}` records name one `dAcPy_c::StateID_*` string in
//     the blob that follows the array (39 such records);
//   * `{0xFFFFFFFF, handler, 0}` records carry a code pointer in `value`
//     (111 such records).
// The string blob starts at `0x80326050`; the next vtable begins at
// `0x803265B0` (base; its slots are `0x803265B8..0x80326614`).
//
// Census of the whole block `0x80325878..0x803265B0`: 846 words (3384 B), 112
// code-pointer entries (1 vtable method + 111 handler values), **100 already
// covered, 12 uncovered**. This pass takes the first ten uncovered entries;
// `0x8013E160` (`0x80325FC8`) and `0x801406E0` (`0x80326034`) remain for a later
// pass. None of the ten is in `functions.tsv`; the extents below come from
// recursive descent (conditional branches and intra-function `b` targets are
// followed, `bl` callees are not, and the walk stops at `bclr`/`bcctr` with LK
// clear).
//
// | entry word | target | extent | role |
// |---|---:|---:|---|
// | `0x80325880` | `0x801446A0` | 64 | deleting destructor (vtable slot `+0x08`) |
// | `0x80325C20` | `0x8012F050` | 4 | `b 0x8012E9A0` forwarder |
// | `0x80325C38` | `0x8012F040` | 4 | `b 0x8012E940` forwarder |
// | `0x80325C44` | `0x8012F0E0` | 4 | `b 0x8012E9A0` forwarder |
// | `0x80325C5C` | `0x8012F0D0` | 4 | `b 0x8012E940` forwarder |
// | `0x80325F14` | `0x8013EA30` | 24 | clear four state words |
// | `0x80325F38` | `0x8013EDF0` | 4 | empty `bclr` stub |
// | `0x80325F5C` | `0x8013EFE0` | 4 | empty `bclr` stub |
// | `0x80325F80` | `0x8013F4C0` | 12 | clear `+0x100C` |
// | `0x80325FA4` | `0x8013DF40` | 8 | tail `0x80056CB0(this, 0xBB)` |
//
// Reused owners: [`FUN_802B9280`] (the module's `operator delete`-style helper)
// and [`crate::game::player::fn_80056cb0`] (status-bit clear). The two
// forwarder targets are not translated and carry no table word of their own, so
// this pass names them as `A248_FN_8012E9A0`/`A248_FN_8012E940` and calls them
// by address.

/// `0x8012E9A0`: shared target of the `0x8012F050`/`0x8012F0E0` forwarders.
///
/// Not in `functions.tsv`, no `fn_<addr>` body, and no table word of its own:
/// the only static references to it are the two 4-byte branches in the
/// `0x80325878` record array. Its own body calls `0x8012E990` (a `b
/// 0x80056CB0` forward that clears status bit `0x18`), tests `+0x14A4`, calls
/// `0x8012E5A0` when it is non-zero, then clears bits `0xAA`, `0x97`, `0x92`
/// and `0x8F` through `0x80056CB0`. It is called by address until a later pass
/// owns it.
const A248_FN_8012E9A0: usize = 0x8012_E9A0;

/// `0x8012E940`: shared target of the `0x8012F040`/`0x8012F0D0` forwarders.
///
/// Not in `functions.tsv` and no table word of its own. Its body is now
/// translated as [`fn_8012e940`]: it calls `0x8012E820(this)`, then **sets**
/// bits `0xAA` and `0x97` through `0x80056C70`. Its neighbour `0x8012E990` is
/// instead a `b 0x80056CB0` forward with `r4 = 0x18`, which the four
/// forwarders do not reach.
const A248_FN_8012E940: usize = 0x8012_E940;

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// 0x801446A0 - 0x80325878 vtable slot 0 (offset +0x08): deleting destructor
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

/// Deleting-destructor tail of the `0x80325878` sub-object.
///
/// The prologue saves `r31` and copies `r3` into it; `cmpi cr0,0,r3,0` +
/// `bc 12,2` returns immediately for a null `this`, and `cmpi cr0,0,r4,0` +
/// `bc 4,1` (branch if `<= 0`) skips the release for a non-positive flag. Only
/// `this != 0 && (int)flag > 0` reaches `bl 0x802B9280`, the module's
/// `operator delete` helper [`FUN_802B9280`] (`0x802B8F70(value, 0)`). `r3` is
/// then reloaded from `r31`, so the receiver is returned verbatim on every path.
///
/// This is the same guard pair as [`fn_8014b430`] (wave 248 lane B, vtable slot
/// 307 of `0x8032679C`); only the vtable that owns the slot differs.
///
/// # Original (untabled)
/// - Address: `0x801446A0`, 64 B (`bclr 20,0` at `0x801446DC`; the next tabled
///   row `0x801446E0` is the 956-byte map-object destructor)
/// - Table: slot 0 of `0x80325878`, i.e. vtable offset `+0x08` (word
///   `0x80325880`); the base words `0x80325878`/`0x8032587C` are the zero
///   offset-to-top and RTTI words
/// - Reach: `vcall(sub-object at object + 0x14FC, 0x08, flag)`
/// - Not in `functions.tsv`; no Ghidra export; no `bl` caller
/// - Prologue `stwu r1,-16`/`mflr` with `r31` saved
///
/// # Arguments
/// - `this`: the secondary sub-object; returned unchanged.
/// - `free_flag`: signed request flag; only a positive value releases `this`.
///
/// # Returns
/// `this`, always - including the null-`this` and non-positive-flag paths.
///
/// # Side effects
/// At most one `0x802B9280(this)` call.
///
/// # Safety
/// `this` must be a live object exposing the `+0x18` release slot that
/// `0x802B9280` dispatches whenever `free_flag > 0`; the object is released
/// after the call.
///
/// # Confidence
/// high - both guards, the saved-register return value and the call target are
/// literal; the "deleting destructor" role follows from the `0x802B9280`
/// operator-delete shape.
pub unsafe fn fn_801446a0(this: usize, free_flag: i32) -> usize {
    if this != 0 && free_flag > 0 {
        platform::call1(FUN_802B9280, this as u32);
    }
    this
}

